WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:02.600
- So, Smartmatic has
made good on its threats

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.632
and is suing Fox News for $2.7 billion

00:00:05.632 --> 00:00:08.810
in an epic, epic complaint.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.530
Now, how epic is this lawsuit?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.197
Well, let me read you one
paragraph from this complaint.

00:00:13.197 --> 00:00:15.300
"The earth is round, two
plus two equals four,

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.780
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris
won the 2020 election

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.830
for President and Vice
President of the United States.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.780
The election was not
stolen, rigged, or fixed.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.613
These are facts.

00:00:22.613 --> 00:00:24.650
They are demonstrable and irrefutable."

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.870
Them are fighting words right there.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.450
For better or worse, this is a complaint

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.500
that was designed to garner attention.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.090
Smartmatic is suing Fox,
Fox News, Lou Dobbs,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.400
Maria Bartiromo, Jeanine
Pirro, Rudy Giuliani,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.770
and Sidney Powell for
collectively $2.7 billion.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.210
Now here's the thing: that
number is completely ridiculous.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.280
It has no basis in fact.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.110
It is designed to generate attention,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.515
but attention this has generated
and Smartmatic is trying

00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:48.877
to undo the damage to its
reputation that was brought

00:00:48.877 --> 00:00:50.500
by all of these people.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.120
This will go down in history as one

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.070
of the most epic complaints
you will ever see in a lawsuit.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.919
So stick around for more
analysis and subscribe

00:00:56.919 --> 00:00:58.553
or I'll see you in court.

